{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3660","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3660","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3660\",\"parent_revision\":\"2854d74b770186ad1edbd5d6d24ebb89db4f2ade61453be3bc0c2b4e35616799\",\"root_revision\":\"2854d74b770186ad1edbd5d6d24ebb89db4f2ade61453be3bc0c2b4e35616799\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-19\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nAfter #3060 was re-groomed on 2026-09-19, new feature-context and architect artifacts were registered under new ids. The 2026-08-20 artifacts (`plan/feature-context-runtime-hints-r7.md`, `plan/architect-runtime-hints-r7.md`) are still registered with `status: current`. The earlier architect artifact leaves open an (a)/(b)/(c) mechanism choice the repo owner has since decided.\\n\\n`artifact_register` accepts `status` (`draft|current|superseded|archived`) but requires `content` (minLength 1) and upserts by (type, id), so changing only the status of an existing artifact means sending its content again. No tool changes the status alone.\\n\\nImpact: `artifact_list` shows superseded design documents as current; later phases list them as prior artifacts and can read a decided question as still open. The orchestrator left them `current` rather than risk overwriting their content.\\n\\nRelated: #2659 (no artifact delete tool).\\n\\nExpected: a caller can mark an existing artifact superseded without resending or changing its content.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation, planning of #3060, 2026-09-20\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-19\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"55ac64ae8f01f1d32eb4d2eaf3bf0dfc1a6b65a8f474c47e290a4bc795ab0db5\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVoHoBg\"}"}